# {{.RenderedProviderName}} Provider

{{ .Description | trimspace }}

## Guides

Start here for managed endpoints. Each guide walks through a working configuration from the repository's `examples/`.

- [Approve AI apps on managed endpoints](guides/endpoint-approved-ai.md): allow the sanctioned AI providers, pin one to its signed desktop app, block the rest.
- [Govern MCP servers on managed endpoints](guides/endpoint-mcp-servers.md): steer sanctioned remote MCP servers through the tenant's gateway, block unvetted ones and known-bad local packages.
- [Block risky tool calls from coding agents](guides/endpoint-tool-calls.md): count, then deny, the commands and tools agents should never run, one device group at a time.
- [Bring an existing endpoint policy under Terraform](guides/endpoint-adopt-existing.md): import what was configured in the admin console, with a first apply that changes nothing.

## Resources and data sources

### AI gateway: LLM and MCP

| Resource | Manages |
| --- | --- |
| [`ferentin_llm_provider`](resources/llm_provider.md) | A tenant binding to an LLM provider, with its credentials (write-only) |
| [`ferentin_llm_policy`](resources/llm_policy.md) | Who may use which LLMs, with limits and routing |
| [`ferentin_mcp_provider`](resources/mcp_provider.md) | A tenant-custom MCP provider in the catalog |
| [`ferentin_mcp_server`](resources/mcp_server.md) | A tenant MCP server: endpoint, upstream auth and routing |
| [`ferentin_mcp_server_from_card`](resources/mcp_server_from_card.md) | An MCP provider and server stamped out from a `server-card.json` |
| [`ferentin_mcp_policy`](resources/mcp_policy.md) | Allow and deny on MCP tools and toolsets, with rate limits |
| [`ferentin_data_protection_policy`](resources/data_protection_policy.md) | Data protection (DLP) on LLM, MCP, A2A and endpoint traffic |
| [`ferentin_edge_site`](resources/edge_site.md) | A site where private service-edge instances enroll and serve traffic |

Lookups: [`ferentin_llm_provider`](data-sources/llm_provider.md), [`ferentin_mcp_provider`](data-sources/mcp_provider.md), [`ferentin_mcp_providers`](data-sources/mcp_providers.md) and [`ferentin_mcp_server_card`](data-sources/mcp_server_card.md) read the global catalogs; [`ferentin_data_protection_profile`](data-sources/data_protection_profile.md), [`ferentin_data_protection_profiles`](data-sources/data_protection_profiles.md), [`ferentin_data_protection_detector`](data-sources/data_protection_detector.md) and [`ferentin_data_protection_detectors`](data-sources/data_protection_detectors.md) read the built-in DLP profiles and detectors.

### Managed endpoints

| Resource | Manages |
| --- | --- |
| [`ferentin_device_group`](resources/device_group.md) | A device group, the targeting unit for endpoint policy |
| [`ferentin_endpoint_destination_rule`](resources/endpoint_destination_rule.md) | Allow or block AI destinations on the device |
| [`ferentin_endpoint_mcp_rule`](resources/endpoint_mcp_rule.md) | Allow, block or steer MCP servers, and block tool calls |
| [`ferentin_endpoint_agent_approval`](resources/endpoint_agent_approval.md) | Approve or deny one catalogued AI agent |
| [`ferentin_endpoint_policy_settings`](resources/endpoint_policy_settings.md) | Posture: what happens when no rule matches, per tenant or device group |

Lists, for finding and importing what exists: [`ferentin_device_groups`](data-sources/device_groups.md), [`ferentin_endpoint_destination_rules`](data-sources/endpoint_destination_rules.md), [`ferentin_endpoint_mcp_rules`](data-sources/endpoint_mcp_rules.md), [`ferentin_endpoint_agent_approvals`](data-sources/endpoint_agent_approvals.md) and [`ferentin_endpoint_policy_settings_scopes`](data-sources/endpoint_policy_settings_scopes.md).

### Identity

| Resource | Manages |
| --- | --- |
| [`ferentin_ai_agent`](resources/ai_agent.md) | An AI agent's OIDC client |
| [`ferentin_workload_identity_provider`](resources/workload_identity_provider.md) | Trust for workload identity tokens from a cloud or CI provider |
| [`ferentin_workload_oauth_client`](resources/workload_oauth_client.md) | An outbound OAuth client for federated upstream MCP auth |

Probes: [`ferentin_workload_identity_provider_test`](data-sources/workload_identity_provider_test.md) and [`ferentin_workload_oauth_client_test`](data-sources/workload_oauth_client_test.md) check a trust configuration or OAuth client against its identity provider on every plan.

